  "_generatedArt": "goods with an `image` are drawn from game/public/assets/goods/<image>.png, produced by tools/gen-art.mjs and cut out by tools/prep-generated.py. Goods without one fall back to a drawn jar in the good's colour.",
  "progression": {
    "_note": "Experience never gets spent, so it is a record of what the farm has done rather than a second currency. Thresholds are cumulative: factor * level * (level - 1). The numbers are set by tools/pace.mjs, which measures how many days of decent play it takes before each crop and animal becomes available at all — content nobody reaches may as well not exist, and a quadratic curve is very easy to write in a way that puts half the game behind a year.",
    "thresholdFactor": 7,
    "xp": {
      "_note": "Weighted so variety pays without becoming compulsory. A twelve-unit order earns one field-worth of picking on top of its money premium — material, and explainable in a sentence. Feeding is once for the whole flock, not once per kind, or keeping one of everything becomes an experience multiplier rather than a choice about farming.",
      "harvestTile": 3,
      "craft": 12,
      "order": 12,
      "feedAll": 8
    },
    "grants": {
      "_note": "The farm itself grows with the level, for ever. Every unlock has a last one, so without this the game stops having anything new to say around level 13 and the level number becomes decoration. Energy and the yard grow without a ceiling because they are one system: each step adds four energy and room for one more of each kind, and feeding four more animals costs about the four energy it just gave, so the day gets larger rather than easier. The barn has a ceiling at barnSoftCapMax times the base, because storage that kept growing would let a player hold half a year of one crop and drip it out under the flooding threshold — which is the exact pressure the market rules exist to apply.",
      "every": 4,
      "energy": 4,
      "barnSoftCap": 8,
      "animalMax": 1,
      "barnSoftCapMax": 3
    },
    "milestoneEvery": 10
  },
